  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "Consider the scores $2, 3, 4, 5, 5, 5, 6, 7, 8$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q6-iqr",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "A score of 23 is added to the dataset. How will this affect the IQR?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The IQR is unchanged at 3.",
          "worked": "Exclude the median when dividing the original nine scores into halves.\n$$\\begin{align*}Q_1&=\\frac{3+4}{2}=3.5\\\\Q_3&=\\frac{6+7}{2}=6.5\\\\\\mathrm{IQR}&=6.5-3.5=3\\end{align*}$$\nAfter adding 23, the ordered scores are $2,3,4,5,5,5,6,7,8,23$. Each half contains five scores.\n$$\\begin{align*}Q_1&=4\\\\Q_3&=7\\\\\\mathrm{IQR}&=7-4=3\\end{align*}$$\nThe IQR remains 3.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q6-explanation",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, describe why the IQR is more useful than the range when there are outliers.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The range increases from 6 to 21, while the IQR remains 3. The IQR measures the spread of the middle 50% of the data and is less affected by outliers.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Original range}&=8-2=6\\\\\\text{New range}&=23-2=21\\end{align*}$$\nThe IQR remains 3. It measures the spread of the middle 50% of the data, so it is less affected by outliers than the range.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
